<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>SRCNN Medical Imaging Enhancement</title>
  <link href="https://stackpath.bootstrapcdn.com/bootstrap/4.5.2/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
  <style>
    body {
      background-color: #f8fafc;
      font-family: 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
      color: #1f2937;
    }

    .navbar {
      background-color: #1e293b;
      color: #fff;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      padding: 1rem 2rem;
    }

    .nav-links {
      display: flex;
      gap: 1.5rem;
      list-style: none;
    }

    .nav-links a {
      color: #fff;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-weight: 500;
    }

    .nav-links a:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .hero {
      text-align: center;
      padding: 100px 20px;
      background: linear-gradient(to right, #2563eb, #1e40af);
      color: #fff;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      font-weight: 800;
      font-size: 3rem;
    }

    .hero p {
      font-size: 1.3rem;
      margin-top: 1rem;
    }

    section {
      padding: 80px 20px;
    }

    .section-title {
      text-align: center;
      font-size: 2rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin-bottom: 30px;
    }

    .line {
      width: 80px;
      height: 4px;
      background-color: #2563eb;
      margin: 10px auto 40px;
    }

    .about p, .methodology p, .results p {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      color: #374151;
    }

    .btn-primary {
      background-color: #2563eb;
      border: none;
      padding: 10px 25px;
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      border-radius: 5px;
    }

    .btn-primary:hover {
      background-color: #1e40af;
    }

    footer {
      background-color: #1e293b;
      color: #fff;
      text-align: center;
      padding: 20px;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
  <!-- Navbar -->
  <nav class="navbar">
    <div class="logo">
      <h3>SRCNN Imaging</h3>
    </div>
    <ul class="nav-links">
      <li><a href="#about">About</a></li>
      <li><a href="#methodology">Methodology</a></li>
      <li><a href="#results">Results</a></li>
      <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <div class="hero">
    <h1>Enhancing Medical Images with SRCNN</h1>
    <p>Super-Resolution Convolutional Neural Network for Improved Diagnostic Clarity</p>
    <a href="#about" class="btn btn-primary mt-4">Learn More</a>
  </div>

  <!-- About Section -->
  <section id="about" class="about">
    <h2 class="section-title">About the Project</h2>
    <div class="line"></div>
    <div class="container">
      <p>
        The SRCNN (Super-Resolution Convolutional Neural Network) project aims to enhance low-resolution medical images 
        such as MRI and CT scans to improve visualization and diagnostic accuracy. This work focuses on applying 
        deep learning-based image super-resolution techniques to reconstruct finer image details and reduce artifacts.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Methodology Section -->
  <section id="methodology" class="methodology bg-light">
    <h2 class="section-title">Methodology</h2>
    <div class="line"></div>
    <div class="container">
      <p>
        Our methodology integrates the Super-Resolution CNN (SRCNN) architecture, consisting of three key layers: 
        patch extraction, non-linear mapping, and reconstruction. The dataset includes medical images preprocessed 
        through normalization and bicubic interpolation. Training is performed using MSE loss and the Adam optimizer 
        for optimal convergence and reconstruction quality.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Results Section -->
  <section id="results" class="results">
    <h2 class="section-title">Results & Insights</h2>
    <div class="line"></div>
    <div class="container text-center">
      <p>
        Experimental results demonstrate that SRCNN effectively restores image sharpness, edges, and fine textures 
        compared to traditional interpolation methods. Quantitative metrics such as PSNR and SSIM show significant 
        improvements in visual fidelity, supporting SRCNN’s potential in clinical imaging applications.
      </p>
      <a href="#contact" class="btn btn-primary mt-3">Get in Touch</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Contact Section -->
  <section id="contact" class="contact bg-light">
    <h2 class="section-title">Contact</h2>
    <div class="line"></div>
    <div class="container text-center">
      <p>
        Interested in collaborating or learning more about this research?  
        <br>Contact the project lead at <strong>vera.nyagaka@strathmore.edu</strong>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer>
    <p>&copy; 2025 SRCNN Medical Imaging Project | Vera Nyagaka</p>
  </footer>

  <script src="https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.5.1.slim.min.js"></script>
  <script src="https://stackpath.bootstrapcdn.com/bootstrap/4.5.2/js/bootstrap.min.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
